&Q000694 = A hymn to Nergal (Nergal B)
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.4.15.2
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.4.15.2&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

1. [ur-saŋ dumu] mah# ni₂ gur₃-ru {d}en-lil₂-la₂
#tr.en: Hero, majestic, awe-inspiring son of @wDN{Enlil}, battering like a storm and roaring against the rebel lands!
#lem: ursaŋ[warrior]; dumu[child]; mah[great]; ni[fear]; gur[lift]; Enlil[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=1

2. [ud-gin₇ ra-ra] ki-bal-še₃ gu₃ ŋar-ra
#tr.en: Immense at his front, at his rear surging as a flood,
#lem: ud[storm]; rah[beat]; kibala[rebel land]; gu[voice]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=2

3. [igi-ni-še₃ u₁₈]-ru bar-ra-ni-še₃ mar-uru₅ zig₃-ga
#tr.en: after he ……,
#lem: igi[eye]; urun[exalted]; bar[outside]; marru[stormwind]; zig[rise]
#etcsl: line-id=3

4. [...] X-ba-ni ki-bi [...]-ge#
#tr.en: …… this place;
#lem: X; X; ki[place]; X
#etcsl: line-id=4

5. [en] {[d]}[meš₃]-lam#-ta-e₃-a ni₂# [huš gur₃-ru]
#tr.en: Lord @wDN{Mešlamta-ea} inspiring terrifying awe,
#lem: en[lord]; Meslamtaea[1]; ni[fear]; huš[reddish]; gur[lift]
#etcsl: line-id=5

6. [X X]-a-ni kur erim₂#-[ŋal₂ nu-ed₂]-de₃
#tr.en: his …… not releasing the hostile land,
#lem: X; X; kur[mountain(s)]; erimŋal[wicked]; e[leave]
#etcsl: line-id=6

7. [si ma-az]-za-ni kalam-[ma ...]-la
#tr.en: his luxuriant horn …… in the Land,
#lem: si[horn]; maz[swell]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; X
#etcsl: line-id=7

8. [...] {ŋiš}tukul# bi-in-sag₃#
#tr.en: struck …… with weapons.
#lem: X; tukul[weapon]; sag[strike]
#etcsl: line-id=8

9. [...] X IM {d}en-[lil₂-le] u₃-tud-da
#tr.en: ……, sired by @wDN{Enlil}, great ……,
#lem: X; X; X; Enlil[1]DN; utud[give birth (to)]
#etcsl: line-id=9

10. [...] GAL X X [mar]-uru₅# X X X
#tr.en: …… flood ……;
#lem: X; X; X; X; marru[stormwind]; X; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=10

11. [...] X X [...]-ŋar#-re-en₆#
#tr.en: he has placed you ……,
#lem: X; X; X; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=11

12. [a₂] nam-ur-saŋ-<ŋa₂>-zu mu-gub-be₂-en₆#
#tr.en: he has positioned you in your heroic strength.
#lem: a[arm]; namursaŋ[heroism]; gub[stand]
#etcsl: line-id=12

13. [saŋ il₂]-la gu₃ ra-bi-da nir-ŋal₂
#tr.en: Raising his head, authoritative with a ringing voice,
#lem: saŋ[head]; il[raise]; gu[voice]; rah[beat]; nirŋal[authoritative]
#etcsl: line-id=13

14. lu₂ zu-me diŋir-re-e-ne-ke₄
#tr.en: knowing the divine powers of the gods,
#lem: lu[person]; zu[know]; diŋir[deity]
#etcsl: line-id=14

15. e₂ |ŊA₂×X|-e ba-[...]-ar kalam-ma-ka
#tr.en: …… of the Land,
#lem: e[house]; X; X; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]
#etcsl: line-id=15

16. an-ne₂# mu#-niŋin₂ niŋ₂-nam#-[ma] a₂ mu-un#-kiŋ₂
#tr.en: he travels through heaven and organises everything.
#lem: an[sky]; niŋin[encircle]; niŋnam[anything]; a[arm]; kiŋ[seek]
#etcsl: line-id=16

17. ud nam-X mu-X X X
#tr.en: When …… you
#lem: ud[sun]; X; X; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=17

18. a-ma#-[ru] kur sig₁₀-sig₁₀-ge₅ mu-ni-dug₄-ga
#tr.en: command the storm which flattens the hostile land,
#lem: amaru[flood]; kur[mountain(s)]; sig[put into]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=18

19. niŋ₂ hul-[ŋal₂]-bi kuš₇ su₃-su₃-me-en
#tr.en: you devastate its evil;
#lem: niŋ[thing]; huluŋal[evil]; kuš[devastation]; su[sink]
#etcsl: line-id=19

20. en-na nu-še-ga#-še₃ su₃-su₃-me-en
#tr.en: you pour it over for as long as it disobeys.
#lem: enna[until]; šeg[agree]; su[sprinkle]
#etcsl: line-id=20

21. ur-saŋ gal# kur-kur-ra#-[me]-en#
#tr.en: You are the great hero of the lands,
#lem: ursaŋ[warrior]; gal[big]; kur[mountain(s)]
#etcsl: line-id=21

22. ŠEŠ-a dub₂-dub₂#-e gu₃ ba-an-de₂-de₂
#tr.en: you speak ……,
#lem: X; dub[tremble]; gu[voice]; de[pour]
#etcsl: line-id=22

23. ŋiri₃ nu-ni#-gub X X-ni-du-un
#tr.en: you go …… where no foot has previously been placed.
#lem: ŋiri[foot]; gub[stand]; X; ŋen[go]
#etcsl: line-id=23

24. šaŋan 7-gin₇ X X-e ba-an-dib
#tr.en: …… like a vessel with seven spouts.
#lem: šaŋan[flask]; n; X; X; dib[pass]
#etcsl: line-id=24

25. saŋ gig₂ teš₂ an-še₃ gu₂ bi₂-in-ŋar
#tr.en: The black-headed gather together at the front.
#lem: saŋ[head]; giggig[black]; teš[unity]; an[sky]; gu[neck]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=25

26. tum₁₂{mušen}-bi-a lal₃-da# zag mi-ni-dib-be₂
#tr.en: You outpace the pigeons with …….
#lem: tum[wild dove]; lal[syrup]; zag[side]; dib[pass]
#etcsl: line-id=26

27. sim{[mušen]} babbar# gig₂#-bi-a zag mi-ni-dib-be₂
#tr.en: You outpace the black and white swallows (?).
#lem: sim[swallow]; babbar[white]; giggig[black]; zag[side]; dib[pass]
#etcsl: line-id=27

28. [X X sila] sig₉-sig₉-ga X [...]
#tr.en: …… in the hushed streets, your …… awesomeness covers the city.
#lem: X; X; sila[street]; sig[silent]; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=28

29. ni₂# X-zu iri mu-un#-[dul]
#tr.en: The majestic and just crown …… your awesomeness.
#lem: ni[fear]; X; iri[city]; dul[cover]
#etcsl: line-id=29

30. men zid# mah ni₂-zu [...]
#tr.en: The …… is a south wind that none can withstand.
#lem: men[tiara]; zid[right]; mah[great]; ni[fear]; X
#etcsl: line-id=30

31. X X u₁₈-lu lu₂-u₃ gaba nu-[mu]-gi₄
#tr.en: At the place of the queen, the most precious place, you exercise the role of supreme deity!
#lem: X; X; ulu[south wind]; lu[person]; gaba[breast]; gi[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=31

32. ki nin ki kal-kal nam-{d}en-lil₂ ša-ba-ak-e
#tr.en: Directing a noble gaze, you exercise kingship in the Land! For his father he has led the people from afar.
#lem: ki[place]; nin[lady]; ki[place]; kal[rare]; namenlil[Enlil-ship]; ak[do]
#etcsl: line-id=32

33. igi saŋ il₂ kalam-ma nam-lugal ša-ba-ak-e
#tr.en: He,
#lem: igi[eye]; saŋ[head]; il[raise]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; namlugal[kingship]; ak[do]
#etcsl: line-id=33

34. a-a-ni-ra uŋ₃ su₃#-ud-bi-ta# mi-ni-ib-e₃
#tr.en: @wDN{Nergal},
#lem: aya[father]; uŋ[people]; sud[distant]; e[leave]
#etcsl: line-id=34

35. kur-ra e₂ X X X ki di#-bi-še₃ i₃-ši#-de₆ {d}nergal-ke₄
#tr.en: has brought them to the …… of the nether world.
#lem: kur[mountain(s)]; e[house]; X; X; X; ki[place]; did[lawsuit]; de[carry]; Nergal[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=35

36. {d}er₃-ra [lugal]-ni# mi₂ na-mu-un-e
#tr.en: Then @wDN{Erra} welcomed his king: @q[Erra,Nergal]{“They have come! You surpass @wDN{An}!
#lem: Erra[1]DN; lugal[king]; mi[cvne]; e[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=36

37. sug₂-sug₂-ge-eš-am₃ an-ra dirig-ga-me-en
#tr.en: Perform the stewardship for @wDN{An} the king!
#lem: sug[stand]; An[1]DN; dirig[make more than]
#etcsl: line-id=37

38. an lugal-e šid du₃-mu-na-ab
#tr.en: In accordance with destiny you determine fates with him, @wDN{Nergal}!”}
#lem: An[1]DN; lugal[king]; šid[recite]; du[build]
#etcsl: line-id=38

39. nam tar-re nam mu-un-di-ni-ib-tar-re {d}nergal-ka-me-en
#tr.en: @wDN{Ninšubur}, the minister of the great place,
#lem: nam[fate]; tar[cut]; nam[fate]; tar[cut]; Nergal[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=39

40. {d}nin-šubur sukkal ki gal kur-ra-ke₄ {d}nergal-ka-ke₄ silim-bi ba-ni-in-dug₄
#tr.en: the underworld, greeted @wDN{Nergal}:
#lem: Ninšubur[1]DN; sukkal[secretary]; ki[place]; gal[big]; kur[mountain(s)]; Nergal[1]DN; silim[healthy]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=40

41. en-e hur-saŋ-ta [lu₂-sa]-gaz ki mu-e₃-a-me-en
#tr.en: @q[Nincubur,Nergal]{“You are the lord who has made the bandits come forth (?) from the mountains.
#lem: en[lord]; hursaŋ[mountain]; sagaz[robber]; ki[place]; e[leave]
#etcsl: line-id=41

42. {d}en#-[lil₂]-gin₇ ki X kur teš₂-a [a₂]-zu# nu-ed₂-de₃
#tr.en: As with @wDN{Enlil} ……,
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; ki[place]; X; kur[mountain(s)]; teš[unity]; a[arm]; e[leave]
#etcsl: line-id=42

43. [ur]-saŋ# [...] gu₂# du₃ {d}en-lil₂-la₂
#tr.en: no part of a foreign land escapes your grasp.
#lem: ursaŋ[warrior]; X; gu[neck]; du[build]; Enlil[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=43

44. [zar-re-eš] {d}en-lil₂-ra ud 1(AŠ)-a du₈-du₈
#tr.en: Hero, for @wDN{Enlil} you piled up @wDN{Enlil's} enemies (?) in a single day.
#lem: zar[sheaf (of barley)]; Enlil[1]DN; ud[sun]; n; du[spread]
#etcsl: line-id=44

45. [... hul] gig# {d}nergal i-zi-gin₇
#tr.en: Hating ……, @wDN{Nergal}, …… as fire,
#lem: X; hulu[bad]; gig[sick]; Nergal[1]DN; izi[fire]
#etcsl: line-id=45

46. [...] kur ud e₃ zig₃-ga-me-en
#tr.en: you rise up in the lands where the sun rises.”}
#lem: X; kur[mountain(s)]; ud[sun]; e[leave]; zig[rise]
#etcsl: line-id=46

47. {[d]}[a-nun-na mu]-un-sug₂-ge-eš
#tr.en: The @wDN{Anuna} gods stepped forward:
#lem: Anunak[1]DN; sug[stand]
#etcsl: line-id=47

48. [...] ki-in-dar sud-sud-gin₇
#tr.en: @q[Anuna,Nergal]{“Like …… cracks ……,
#lem: X; kindar[hole]; sud[distant]
#etcsl: line-id=48

49. [...] X-a-ni {d}nergal-ka-me-en
#tr.en: ……, you are @wDN{Nergal}!”}
#lem: X; X; Nergal[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=49

